{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And I charged your judges.</b> I said to them: be deliberate in judgment — if a case comes before you once, twice, and three times, do not say, 'This case has already come before me many times'; rather, keep deliberating in it (there)." "<b>At that time.</b> From when I appointed them, I said to them: Now is not like the past — in the past you were under your own authority; now you are subject to the public (there)." "<b>Hear.</b> A present-tense form; אודנ\"ט בְּלַעַ\"ז — like זָכוֹר, שָׁמוֹר." "<b>And between his neighbor.</b> This is his adversary in the case, who harbors things against him. Another interpretation: <b>and between his neighbor</b> — even concerning matters of dwelling, such as division between brothers, even between an oven and a stove (there; Sanhedrin 7)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {2 "the la'az is Old French oïr/entendre, 'to hear' (present participle)."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:29.265480392Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}